MDMI Mega Drive
https://github.com/KPY7030P/mdmi-plugin

An unofficial plugin built on the Mega Drive MIDI Interface by Robert Hargreaves
and the BlastEm emulator by Michael Pavone. It is not made or endorsed by them.

The plugin's own code: Copyright (C) 2026 KPY7030P (Trojan_247). It is free
software under the GNU General Public License as published by the Free
Software Foundation, version 3 or (at your option) any later version; see
LICENSE. The plugin as distributed includes the MDMI ROM (GPL-3.0) and is
therefore under GPL-3.0.

Modified third-party code (GPL-3.0, section 5a). The changes are kept as
patches against the pinned upstream commits in tools/deps.lock:

- BlastEm, fork https://github.com/ulalume/blastem at commit 5702187, modified
  by patches/0001-mdmi-everdrive-bridge.patch, changed 2026-11-02 to 2026-11-07:
  MIDI and audio pass between the plugin and the emulated cartridge, and the
  JIT memory is freed on unload.
- Mega Drive MIDI Interface v1.34 (commit 6cfe921), modified by
  patches/0003-mdmi-psg-envelopes.patch, changed 2026-11-04 to 2026-11-08:
  PSG envelopes stored by SysEx, PSG restored after DAC switches, note stack
  and DAC notes, one-shot samples. tools/build_plugin.sh builds it with the
  name "v1.34p", which its screen shows.
- clap-wrapper v0.17.0 (commit 806bba0, MIT), modified by
  patches/0002-clap-wrapper.patch, changed 2026-11-04.

